            ]
          },
          "worked": "Each exponential branch is continuous on its own interval. At the joining point,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\lim_{x\\to0^-}f(x)&=e^{0+1}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to0^-}f(x)&=e\\\\f(0)&=k(0.5^0)\\\\f(0)&=k\\end{align*}$$\nThe right-hand limit also equals $k$. Therefore continuity requires $k=e$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
